name conversation_burst_loss
describe User <-> AI conversation, audio, 100 ms RTT, 5% loss in bursts (mean burst 5 packets) each way (#757)
call two-way
video off
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=50ms queue=300ms loss=5% burst=5
reverse at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=50ms queue=300ms loss=5% burst=5
turn user 1s-4s
turn ai after=800ms len=4s
turn user 10s-13s
turn ai after=800ms len=4s
turn user 19s-22s
turn ai after=800ms len=4s
# program.md 6.3, conversation rows (5% loss, here in bursts): every reply heard (sev:1), at most 500 ms added (sev:2).
expect conv.responses == 3
expect conv.response_delay_p95_ms < 500
# No line on conv.user_speech_lost_pct here (program.md 6.3: at most 2%). Owner decision (2026-11-01, #965): 5% loss in
# bursts of 5 packets is outside where 2% holds. Measured on 20 seeds: 3.05% mean at the AI's playout; deeper RED (#965)
# reached a 2.0% mean (worst 3.7%); audio NACK (#971, `up_audio_nack on`, off by default) brings the speech the AI
# receives within 500 ms to a 1.1% mean (worst 4.4%), which is the option for native clients.
